{"title":"Simson line","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">geometry</a>, given a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> ABC and a point P on its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcircle\" title=\"Circumcircle\">circumcircle</a>, the three closest points to P on lines AB, AC, and BC are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Collinear\" title=\"Collinear\">collinear</a> and form a <b>Simson line</b>.\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Simsonline.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d8/Simsonline.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"397\" height=\"417\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Definition_of_this_line\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Definition of this line</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Proof_of_existence\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof of existence</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Simson_line_of_a_complete_quadrilateral\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Simson line of a complete quadrilateral</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition_of_this_line\">Definition of this line</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Simson_line&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition of this line\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Simson_line.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e5/Simson_line.png/270px-Simson_line.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"270\" height=\"260\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e5/Simson_line.png/405px-Simson_line.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e5/Simson_line.png/540px-Simson_line.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Simson_line_inverse.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/c9/Simson_line_inverse.png/270px-Simson_line_inverse.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"270\" height=\"263\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/c9/Simson_line_inverse.png/405px-Simson_line_inverse.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/c9/Simson_line_inverse.png/540px-Simson_line_inverse.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be given.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12e13563a6df1a207dad9672dd7b73df2a96faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D, E,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foots of the perpendiculars dropped from P to lines AB, AC, and BC, respectively.\n</p><p>Then points  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12e13563a6df1a207dad9672dd7b73df2a96faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D, E,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear iff the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919b9f77a6985e760286799909be5bfe0152f40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_of_existence\">Proof of existence</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Simson_line&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof of existence\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be on the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919b9f77a6985e760286799909be5bfe0152f40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/9782b1e2d5b2564ccac4ed8691d606ded8185133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BFP = \\angle BDP = 90^\\circ \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"234\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ecb2baab21332a9a3103d0a7275f9abcad65344.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BPDF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0de7bbdf6c729fdcf9f20a65c3971687d4490c90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle PDF = 180^\\circ – \\angle CBP.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"231\" height=\"15\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/6/d36b7405237df2ae57efda1a08f9f1ed67a85f5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADP = \\angle AEP = 90^\\circ \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"232\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc255f0da8748662e590527b416392f236fab92d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEPD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/77915d70f1d85482e77ead9c291d5be5c2b3a1f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle PDE = \\angle PAE.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"188\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/b/40ba04bf4b374bcd64002038bccc449508343a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACBP$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/3/523ce6a222a34550c33a6b1db6a57ddd225dfcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle PBC = \\angle PAE \\implies \\angle PDF + \\angle PDE = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"426\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47a70cf0c86ef38f2dd0ae3c19ab80e8814d118.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies D, E,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear as desired. \n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>Let the points  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12e13563a6df1a207dad9672dd7b73df2a96faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D, E,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be collinear. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc255f0da8748662e590527b416392f236fab92d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEPD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a86ea4e2e7ac4231bb8a98949a05fe7a6b84ebeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle APE = \\angle ADE, \\angle DPE = \\angle BAC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"331\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c07012a2bdfb9e2303ad6711c39effc903c1ba2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BFDP$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/9676541f305e4e9ecf5d2acd0ad7d99d2aa824dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\angle BPF = \\angle BDF, \\angle DPF = \\angle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"330\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce177a82e3cad5acb3066e8cc54d9a1aed50e07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADE = \\angle BDF \\implies \\angle BPA = \\angle EPF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"325\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/1/4917a1744a7b28a873d5b3038fbb3b7e985b3db6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\angle BAC + \\angle ABC = 180^\\circ – \\angle ACB \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"323\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/b/40ba04bf4b374bcd64002038bccc449508343a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACBP$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is cyclis as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Simson_line_of_a_complete_quadrilateral\">Simson line of a complete quadrilateral</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Simson_line&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Simson line of a complete quadrilateral\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Simson_complite.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/3e/Simson_complite.png/430px-Simson_complite.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"430\" height=\"230\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/3e/Simson_complite.png/645px-Simson_complite.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/3e/Simson_complite.png/860px-Simson_complite.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let four lines made four triangles of a complete quadrilateral. In the diagram these are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d15ba44fecfa3229692453358049c41718818e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, \\triangle ADE, \\triangle CEF, \\triangle BDF.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"264\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the Miquel point of a complete quadrilateral.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/4/854274ff024657e55a2516f8f7f5b2aab8050a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K, L, N,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foots of the perpendiculars dropped from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/f/e0faef226f6b9d1f294755e0eefe3893bea2e9db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, AC, EF,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/1/ce1f5a2ad34bb6fb5169f99e437b9f3e21d1887e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>Prove that points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/877540269e85610e41d970e0edcbaeb049464775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K,L, N,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Simson_line&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> be the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/8/fa8d4111dc0231b4a5af585d9b2248227a401f17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, \\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> be the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71d8bbdf41238f00829cf9b922c23cb9495bdf6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CEF.$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/d/45d579d0b67b22f67f2f4d95a91fcd6284b0068c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = \\Omega \\cap \\omega.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/2058fb2fac59b6c8536586e65d1a83554090676f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K, L,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear as Simson line of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919b9f77a6985e760286799909be5bfe0152f40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e4974e2530780abdf12d75102ef783f81ad871a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L, N,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear as Simson line of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71d8bbdf41238f00829cf9b922c23cb9495bdf6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CEF.$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Therefore points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/4/854274ff024657e55a2516f8f7f5b2aab8050a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K, L, N,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear, as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Simson_line&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Problem_on_Simson_line.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/db/Problem_on_Simson_line.png/400px-Problem_on_Simson_line.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"227\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/db/Problem_on_Simson_line.png/600px-Problem_on_Simson_line.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/db/Problem_on_Simson_line.png/800px-Problem_on_Simson_line.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<ul><li>Let the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf6d387ce491c0ca100c134021f21f616d75162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be collinear and the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe92ce71245df468e3fc740e3d68ddeaefbddaf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P \\notin AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/6133274a1790c342b36ae860a425788b8a3427eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O,O_0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> be the circumcenters of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f24a1a2f0aaa1801497a9bf1a18b7ee9843cde2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABP, \\triangle ACP,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bfc7b6d29dae3f7d49733e6d8f1eb691af4e6ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/e/12ec9523355e760d9839706e0d313cab8bd96976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OO_0O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li><ul><li>Solution</li></ul></li></ul>\n<dl><dd>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12e13563a6df1a207dad9672dd7b73df2a96faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D, E,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoints of segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/2/aa25a3dabae9462c82026ab54174ddf5a3da8c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, AC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/1/ce1f5a2ad34bb6fb5169f99e437b9f3e21d1887e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. Then points  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12e13563a6df1a207dad9672dd7b73df2a96faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D, E,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/3/573567d2c5af099b8bcbf94be7ae9a6f3b66aa77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(DE||AB, EF||DC).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" /></dd></dl>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d992a8e83bc0eea12b6ff2b4dc913b814317857.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PD \\perp OO_0, PE \\perp OO_1, PF \\perp O_0O_1 \\implies\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is Simson line of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/1/ac13cb8abd12be083d2980eb19476cc42ded7603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OO_0O_1 \\implies P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" /> lies on circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/e/12ec9523355e760d9839706e0d313cab8bd96976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OO_0O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> as desired.</dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Simson_line&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Miquel%27s_point\" title=\"Miquel&#39;s point\">Miquel's point</a></li>\n<li><